y-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\nFixes #102818\r\n\r\nThis should fix a lot of issues relating to StyleBoxFlat producing glitchy overlapping shapes. It does this by reducing the inner corner radii proportionately to how much they cause overflows (when the borders + radii are bigger than the available rect).\r\n\r\n| Before | After |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5bd2dfea-096b-45a6-ac2f-d80c924cd00c) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/239c4d4a-192b-44d6-8649-a8b3fff1f126) |\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d7bf47a-b8af-47ff-9e77-7b7b30c486bf) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a5703cc-d0f9-4f99-a543-962789d20c68) |\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18a5db2f-6c0f-417c-ac4e-a38c797d17e9) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6bade3a3-51df-457a-8c6a-1361af77fa63) |\r\n\r\nIt's worth noting that anti aliasing is a separate issue and can still sometimes cause tiny bands to appear with translucent colors. I (or someone else) can try to tackle that in another PR. For example:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b2d27eb-19f8-457b-892f-fa10527c1d5c)\r\n\r\nEdit: Corners now scale down instead of reducing their radius","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null